## Common Patterns

### Toast Notifications
```typescript
const { addToast } = useToast();
addToast({ type: 'success', message: 'Saved!' });
```

### Error Handling
```typescript
try {
  await save(data);
  addToast({ type: 'success', message: 'Saved!' });
} catch (error) {
  if (isApiError(error)) {
    addToast({ type: 'error', message: error.statusText });
  }
}
```

## Constraints

### ❌ NEVER
- `any` type, `React.FC`, inline styles
- Tailwind, Material-UI, Chakra, Ant Design
- react-router-dom (use wouter)
- React Query (use SWR)
- Redux/MobX (use Jotai minimal)
- jsdom as default (use happy-dom)

### ✅ ALWAYS
- Explicit types, CSS Modules, design tokens
- Error boundaries, loading states
- ARIA labels, semantic HTML
- Atomic commits, JSDoc for public APIs

